<title>FRANCE: CDC denies it selling Canal Plus stake.</title>
<headline>CDC denies it selling Canal Plus stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial institution CDC said it had no intention to sell its stake in Canal Plus to Havas, as rumoured in the Le Monde newspaper, while Havas said it was not in the market to buy.</p>
<p>The Caisse des Depots et Consignations (CDC) had a seven percent direct stake in Canal Plus and its Partcom investment vehicle another 3.5 percent. These percentages are before the planned merger with Dutch-based Nethold.</p>
<p>&quot;I have no intention of selling my shares,&quot; said Willy Stricker, chairman of PartCom.</p>
</text>
